class:: BlipDisp
summary:: Equal-magnitude harmonics with quadratic spectral phase
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/BlipExtensions, Classes/BlipAD, Classes/BlipDecay, Classes/BlipDiff, Classes/BlipFB, Classes/BlipFrac, Classes/BlipInt, Classes/BlipKernel, Classes/BlipPM, Classes/BlipPeak, Classes/BlipPower, Classes/BlipSeries, Classes/BlipWidth

description::

BlipDisp sums code::cos(k * phase + dispersion * k.squared):: for the retained
harmonics. Dispersion changes spectral phase only: the static harmonic
magnitudes remain equal.

This is an intentionally O(N) oscillator. Quadratic phase coefficients are
generated by a stable recurrence into constructor-allocated banks, and a
single oscillator recurrence supplies harmonic phase. Changes to dispersion
or effective count crossfade between banks for one block. Dispersion is
sampled once per block, wrapped modulo code::2pi::, and the requested count is
limited to 2048. Since static dispersion changes phase rather than frequency,
it creates no extra partials; the retained carrier set is limited below
Nyquist.

The closest vanilla comparison is link::Classes/DynKlang::. Both can assign
partial phase, but BlipDisp generates the structured quadratic law internally
and supports a runtime Nyquist-limited count.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Frequency in Hz. Audio or control rate; signed values are valid.

argument:: numharm
Requested harmonic count, sampled once per block and clipped to code::1..2048::
before limiting.

argument:: dispersion
Quadratic phase coefficient in radians, sampled once per block. Audio-rate
modulation is not supported.

argument:: mul
Post-processing multiplier.

argument:: add
Post-processing offset.

examples::

code::
(
{ BlipDisp.ar(70, 80, 0.01, 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{ BlipDisp.ar(40, 120, LFNoise1.kr(0.2).range(-0.03, 0.03), 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
// Modulating all parameters for a dynamic sound
(
{ BlipDisp.ar(MouseX.kr(50, 500, 'exponential'), MouseY.kr(1, 100), LFNoise1.kr(0.5).range(-0.1, 0.1)) ! 2 * 0.1 }.play;
)
::
